"Licensor" means ihatectf, the copyright holder granting this License.

"Individual" means a natural person acting solely in that person's personal
capacity and not on behalf of, at the direction of, or for the benefit of any
company, employer, client, partnership, association, government, school,
university, laboratory, nonprofit, or other organization.

"Official Repository" means the public GitHub repository that the Licensor
identifies as the canonical repository for Hatifect.

"Software" means the copyrightable source code, object code, binaries, assets,
documentation, and other materials contained in the Official Repository, and
builds and Modifications of those materials, but only to the extent owned by or
licensable by the Licensor. Software does not include Third-Party Components or
User Materials.

"Third-Party Component" means any material identified as being governed by a
license or rights holder other than the Licensor. Third-Party Components remain
subject exclusively to their applicable terms.

"User Materials" means an Individual's original configurations, save data,
logs, reports, recordings, and other content created through use of the
Software, except for any Software or copyrightable Hatifect material included
in them.

"Modification" means any adaptation, alteration, translation, arrangement, or
other derivative work of the Software that requires copyright permission.

"Private Use" means use solely by one Individual, on that Individual's own
devices or through an Authorized Service Provider, without access by any other
person except the provider's systems and personnel to the minimum extent
necessary to provide the authorized service, and without any Commercial,
Professional, or Organizational Use.

"Commercial Use" means use intended for or directed toward commercial
advantage, monetary compensation, revenue generation, sale, licensing, or the
provision of paid goods or services. Creation and ordinary monetization of
Permitted Media under Section 5 is not Commercial Use of the Software.

"Professional Use" means use in carrying out employment, contract work,
consulting, a trade, or a profession, whether or not compensation is received
for the particular use.

"Organizational Use" means use by, for, at the direction of, or for the benefit
of any legal entity, group, institution, employer, client, school, university,
laboratory, nonprofit, government, or other organization.

"Authorized Service Provider" means a storage, backup, build, or artificial-
intelligence service used only as a technical processor on behalf of the
Individual, with access restricted to what is reasonably necessary to provide
that service. An artificial-intelligence service qualifies only if its terms or
applicable settings prohibit use of the submitted Software to train, retrain,
fine-tune, evaluate, or improve any model other than transient processing
strictly necessary to respond to the Individual.

"Contribution" means code, documentation, assets, or another Modification
intentionally submitted to the Official Repository through an Issue, feature
branch, or pull request under Section 6.

"Accepted Contribution" means a Contribution merged into a branch of the
Official Repository by the Licensor or by a person expressly authorized by the
Licensor to perform that merge.

"Permitted Media" means screenshots, video, livestreams, reviews, commentary,
and demonstrations depicting the Software or its operation, but not material
that contains substantial source code or makes protected Hatifect assets
available for extraction or reuse other than as incidental to the depiction.

2. Limited personal-use permission

Subject to every term of this License, the Licensor grants an Individual a
limited, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and non-
sublicensable permission, for the duration of copyright unless terminated, to:

- view the Software in the Official Repository;
- download the Software and keep private copies on the Individual's own
  devices;
- keep access-controlled copies with an Authorized Service Provider solely for
  private storage or backup;
- privately reproduce, modify, commit, compile, test, and run the Software for
  the Individual's personal, non-commercial purposes, including personal
  learning, research, and benchmarking; and
- provide only the portions reasonably necessary to an Authorized Service
  Provider for those permitted purposes.

An Authorized Service Provider receives no independent license or right in the
Software. The Individual is responsible for the provider's compliance and must
remove provider-held copies when they are no longer reasonably needed.

3. GitHub platform and contribution permission

GitHub's terms for public repositories may grant Users rights to view and fork
public repository content through GitHub's functionality. Nothing in this
License restricts rights granted directly by GitHub or by applicable law.

In addition, an Individual may use GitHub to create a fork, feature branch,
commits, and a pull request containing Modifications, solely and reasonably as
necessary to propose a Contribution to the Official Repository. This permission
includes the public display and reproduction inherent in that GitHub workflow.
It does not permit releases, packages, mirrors, GitHub Pages deployments,
standalone patch archives, binary distributions, or publication on another
service or repository.

The Individual may not commit directly to a protected primary branch of the
Official Repository unless the Licensor has expressly granted that access.
Granting branch access does not grant authority to merge a pull request.

4. Issues and technical discussion

An Individual may open and participate in Issues in the Official Repository and
may include descriptions, reasonably limited diagnostic logs, screenshots, and
the minimum source-code excerpts necessary to explain a problem. Secrets,
credentials, personal data, and unrelated confidential information must be
removed. Full modified files, complete patches, and substantial portions of the
Software must be submitted through the contribution workflow in Section 3, not
through an Issue.

Security vulnerabilities are governed by Section 9 and must not be reported in
a public Issue before coordinated disclosure is permitted.

5. Permitted Media and attribution

An Individual may create, publish, and monetize Permitted Media. Monetization
may include platform advertising, sponsorships, subscriptions, and donations,
provided that the Permitted Media is not used to sell the Software, provide
paid access to the Software, or distribute any copy or Modification.
Notwithstanding the definitions and restrictions concerning Commercial Use and
Professional Use, creating and monetizing Permitted Media in compliance with
this Section is expressly permitted. This exception does not authorize
Organizational Use of the Software.

Every publication of Permitted Media must include, in a reasonably prominent
location such as its description or credits:

- the name "Hatifect";
- the name "ihatectf" as the project author; and
- a working link to the Official Repository, where the format supports links.

This permission does not grant any right to imply sponsorship, endorsement, or
affiliation with the Licensor.

6. Contributions

6.1 Submission and review

By intentionally submitting a Contribution, the contributor represents that
the contributor has the legal right to submit it, that it does not knowingly
contain another person's confidential information, and that all included
Third-Party Components and applicable license terms have been clearly
identified.

Until a Contribution is accepted, the contributor grants the Licensor a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to host, reproduce, display,
test, analyze, comment on, and modify the Contribution solely for review and
evaluation. The contributor may withdraw an unaccepted Contribution by closing
the pull request and clearly notifying the Licensor before merge. Withdrawal
ends this review license prospectively, but does not require deletion of GitHub
records, backups, discussions, or copies that GitHub may lawfully retain under
its terms.

6.2 Accepted Contributions

Upon merge, the contributor retains copyright in the contributor's original
material and grants the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, fully
paid-up, non-exclusive, irrevocable, transferable, and sublicensable copyright
license to use, reproduce, modify, prepare derivative works of, combine,
publicly display, publicly perform, distribute, make available, commercialize,
and license or relicense the Accepted Contribution, in source or object form,
under any terms chosen by the Licensor.

The contributor also grants the Licensor and recipients of software authorized
by the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, fully paid-up, non-
exclusive, irrevocable patent license to make, have made, use, offer to sell,
sell, import, and otherwise transfer the Accepted Contribution, but only under
patent claims controlled by the contributor that are necessarily infringed by
the Accepted Contribution alone or by its combination with the Software to
which it was submitted. This patent license terminates for a contributor who
initiates patent litigation alleging that the Software or the Accepted
Contribution infringes a patent.

The Licensor will use reasonable efforts to preserve contributor authorship in
Git commit metadata. The Licensor may squash, rebase, edit, combine, or
relicense commits and is not required to provide attribution elsewhere.

6.3 Acceptance control

The Licensor alone decides whether, when, and in what form to accept, modify,
reject, or close a Contribution. Submission creates no obligation to respond,
provide reasons, merge the Contribution, or continue development.

If a Contribution is withdrawn or rejected, the contributor retains rights in
the contributor's original material. The contributor receives no additional
right to distribute, publish, or use Hatifect-derived material outside the
permissions of this License.

