9. Coordinated security disclosure

An Individual may privately investigate the Software for security
vulnerabilities within the permissions of this License. A vulnerability must be
reported through the private security-reporting channel identified in the
Official Repository, or through another private contact method designated by
the Licensor.

Public disclosure is permitted on the earlier of:

- the Licensor's public release of a fix;
- the Licensor's written authorization; or
- 90 days after the Licensor receives a sufficiently detailed private report
  that reasonably enables investigation of the vulnerability.

Disclosure must be limited to what is reasonably necessary to explain and
verify the vulnerability and must not include unrelated or excessive portions
of the Software. Nothing in this Section restricts a disclosure required by
applicable law, but advance notice to the Licensor must be given when legally
permitted.

